    <hr />

    <h2>The moment everything changed</h2>
    <p>In 2018, Magie and I became parents. With the arrival of our second son, we set professional bridge aside. In 2023, I played a tournament with my mother. Our sons — three and five at the time — asked what I had been doing. They wanted to try it themselves. And so our boys played their very first hand of bridge.</p>
    <p>I watched how quickly they picked it up, how they thought, how much fun they had. Something clicked. I realized I could combine my three greatest passions: teaching, young people, and bridge.</p>

    <h2>The career switch — three passions, one mission</h2>
    <p>In 2024 I made the leap. I left my job as a lawyer with the Dutch government and took the plunge. I dedicated myself fully to youth bridge and started teaching at schools. My enthusiasm and the progress we made caught the attention of the Dutch Bridge Federation, who asked me to organize the national schools' bridge championship as project coordinator — and growth exceeded every expectation. In the first year, 101 pupils from 17 schools took part. The year after: 268 pupils from 34 schools. My students from De Agnietenschool (Elburg) and De Marshof (Zwolle) placed first and second in the primary-school category of the 2026 national schools' bridge championship.</p>
    <p>Youth bridge had been declining in the Netherlands for years. That tide is turning — and I'm proud to be part of that.</p>

    <h2>Why I coach</h2>
    <p>I've been teaching students, beginners and advanced players since 2000. Since 2012 I've run clinics at bridge clubs across the Netherlands. But the deepest motivation is simple: it gives me enormous satisfaction to contribute to someone's development. Watching someone grow because of what we did together — that's what I do it for. That's something I'm genuinely proud of.</p>

    <h2>My approach</h2>
    <div class="principle-box">"Complexity is the enemy of execution."</div>
    <p>I work with general principles you can apply anywhere. Bridge is a logical game. I don't teach you rules — I teach you how to reason through any problem using logic. I give you room to discover things for yourself and step in where needed, always in a friendly way that respects who you are. Practical, effective, results-driven.</p>

